 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Read the question",
   "text": "Define the **internal energy** of a system and show how it is related to the absolute temperature.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "T": 300
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "Definition",
   "text": "**Internal energy** \\( U \\) is the **sum of all the molecular energies**, kinetic and potential, of the substance.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "T": 300
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "Ideal gas: kinetic only",
   "text": "In an **ideal gas** the collisions are perfectly elastic and the molecules exert **no forces** on each other, so there is no potential energy. \\( U \\) is just the **translational kinetic energy** of the molecules.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "T": 300
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "Energy of one molecule",
   "text": "Kinetic theory gives the mean kinetic energy of one molecule: \\[ \\left\\langle \\tfrac{1}{2}mv^{2} \\right\\rangle = \\tfrac{3}{2}\\,kT \\] so it is proportional to the **kelvin** temperature.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "T": 300
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "Energy of N molecules",
   "text": "\\[ U = N \\cdot \\tfrac{3}{2}kT \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad U \\propto T \\] Raise \\( T \\) and watch the bar of \\( U \\) grow in proportion.",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "T": 300
     },
     "at": 0
    },
    {
     "tween": {
      "T": 450
     },
     "at": 0,
     "dur": 4500
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "title": "Sign of ΔU, and real gases",
   "text": "\\( \\Delta U = U_2 - U_1 \\) is **positive** when \\( T \\) rises, **negative** when \\( T \\) falls and **zero** when \\( T \\) is constant. For a **real** gas, \\( U \\) also contains potential energy, so it depends on \\( T \\) and \\( V \\).",
   "actions": [
    {
     "set": {
      "T": 450
     },
     "at": 0
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "readouts": [
  {
   "label": "Temperature (K)",
   "value": "{{T|0}}",
   "role": "hot"
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
